Subject: [PATCH] Milestone 8: optional science overlays (Diviner PRP,
 ShadowCam) and URL-hash race fix

- Feasibility audit of Diviner, LEND, Mini-RF, M3, ShadowCam and CRaTER over
  verified HTTPS; integrated, deferred and rejected layers documented
- Reusable per-site science layer framework (index.json + Uint16 layers on
  mesh vertices, model/observation kind, coded states, provenance, caveats)
- Diviner Polar Resource Products (model-derived Tmax, Tavg at 2 cm, ice
  stability depth) at all three 5 m sites; undocumented -1 code kept as a
  separate, uninterpreted state
- ShadowCam controlled Shackleton mosaic (observed I/F) where it covers
- UI: layer toggle, opacity, legend with units, badges, readout, sources
- Validation: brute-force triangle containment, source pixels, PSR cross-
  check (Tmax 87.6 K in PSR vs 279.5 K outside)
- Fix: hashchange handler reads HashChangeEvent.newURL so a pending state
  commit cannot overwrite an edited/pasted link
- Docs: MILESTONE8_ACCEPTANCE.md, PROJECT_STATUS, DATA_SOURCES, AI_USAGE,
  README

